NOS Report Guide 
Abstract 
NOSs are statements that define the performance standards individuals must achieve 
when carrying out workplace functions, along with the necessary underpinning 
knowledge and understanding. 
The apprentice must understand the performance standards and apply the tasks 
assigned to him in accordance with those standards. 
Five NOS reports are required to be submitted, categorized as follows 
 4 Technical NOSs. 
 1 Non-Technical NOS (Soft Skills). 
Technical NOSs: These standards focus on industry-specific expertise, such as 
programming, networking, data analysis, engineering, or system maintenance, ensuring 
professionals meet occupational requirements and best practices. 
Non-technical NOSs: These standards cover communication, teamwork, leadership, 
problem-solving, adaptability, and time management, ensuring individuals have 
interpersonal and cognitive skills for eAective collaboration. 
The NOSs can be found on this site: https://www.ukstandards.org.uk/en 
1 
How to Find specific NOS 
Enter Keywords or URN 
National Occupational Standards (NOS) can 
be identified using a Unique Registration 
Number (URN) for precise searches. 
Alternatively, keywords may be used to 
generate broader search results. 
Select a Business Sector (Suite) 
NOS are categorized into suites based on the 
industry sector they apply to. The number of 
NOS within each suite varies according to 
sector-specific requirements. 
Select an Occupation 
NOS are developed in alignment with specific 
occupations. Searching by occupation 
provides a wider range of relevant results. 
The matching NOSs will be displayed upon completing the search process: 
2 
Read the performance section points, check how they align with the work tasks, then 
copy them into the NOS Report template and explain below each one how it was applied, 
supported by evidence. 
3 


doc sample

•	Student Name: Abdallah Daradkeh
•	Company: Publicis Groupe
•	Number of NOS: TECHDUBI1
•	Name of NOS: Create business insight dashboards and reports
 **Performance criteria of the NOS and how you applied it in your company ** 
  (Explain and include evidence from your work)  
P1 – Identify customer requirements to plan dashboard or reporting solutions
I go through many trailhead modules, and learnt theoretical and practical to identify requirements to plan dashboard and reporting solutions. I studied, analyzed and creating dashboards and reports for many Systems included in the system
 
 
 
 
P2 – Select the specified data to produce reports and dashboards

I selected the required Salesforce data needed to create reports and dashboards, such as Accounts, Leads, Opportunities, and related fields. I also filtered the data based on the reporting purpose, for example by status, date, owner, or record type, to make sure the report shows only the relevant information.
   

P3 – Create and modify data reports and dashboards using industry standard tools to provide business insights
I created and modified reports and dashboards in Salesforce by choosing the needed fields, applying filters, and organising the report layout. I also worked with dashboard components to display the data visually and support better understanding of business performance.
 
 
   	

P4 – Assist in providing performance metrics across the reporting suite to inform stakeholders
I helped prepare reporting metrics in Salesforce by using reports and dashboards to display useful information such as totals, filtered results, and record statuses. This supports stakeholders by giving them a clear view of performance and progress.
P5 – Deliver ad hoc reports in line with organisational requirements
I delivered ad hoc reports by creating or modifying Salesforce reports according to specific business requirements, ensuring that the selected data, filters, and report layout matched the requested information.

P6 – Distribute reports and dashboards to stakeholders in line with organisational procedures

I supported this criterion by preparing Salesforce reports and dashboards to be ready for sharing with relevant stakeholders. I ensured the reports were organised, updated, and followed the required data structure and access considerations.
P7 – Distribute reports and dashboards to stakeholders in line with organisational procedures

I applied this criterion partially by learning how Salesforce Digital Experience can be used to provide online access to Salesforce information. I also understood the importance of following organisational procedures, permissions, and security rules before publishing any reports or dashboards online.

